Argh, playing the game of my life: level 30, max stats in everything,
over 35 million points worth of gems on one of the upper levels,
abusing every spoiler in existence; and I was upping my hit points
with some reverse-genocided nurses. Oops, a green dragon came along,
which I killed, but afterwards (don't know if related to the dragon or
not) one of the nurses wasn't moving, as if it was asleep. I couldn't
get her to attack me, even when I hit her, although I could still get
the "relax this won't hurt a bit" message when #chat'ting with her.
Didn't know what to do, so I went to kill her. At the final blow by my
+8 Excalibur, the screen blanked and I got the message:

Contact <whoever> and it may be possible to rebuild.--More--
Error: relmon not found.--More--
Bad fruit #1?  Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better Quit.--More--
Do you want your possessions identified [ynq] y
Weapons:
.
. <- only single dots here, none of my stuff was mentioned.
.
Armor:
.
.
.

I was on level 11 when the panic occurred, and when the screen
reappeared when it asked me if I wanted to see my intrinsics, it
showed one of the maze levels from deep down in the dungeon rather
than the normal rooms from dlvl 11. The high score entry was:

 No  Points     Name                                                   Hp [max]
  8    1452678  pullen-E died on dungeon level 11 [max 50].           700 [700]
                Panic.

Fortunately, the program left a #####pullen.e.Z file in the save
directory, which I renamed to #####pullen.Z I restarted nethack, and
the game was back to normal, as if no problem had ever occured. Whew,
thought I had lost the game there for a while. I've forwarded this
message to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu (even though work on 3.0 is
apparently done, and yes I still have the .e file) but thought I'd
post it to the net as a warning and to see if anyone knows what's
wrong or has encountered it themselves. (This is standard 3.0 pl10.)

